      "content": "Absolutely, this is a critical and complex aspect of forensic linguistics and social psychology. Dialect and speech patterns are inextricably linked to race and ethnic identity in the eyes of many listeners. Juries risk projecting deeply ingrained racial stereotypes onto the speaker's language, moving the focus away from the evidence and onto preconceived notions about the witness's group identity. This exposure to systemic bias means that linguistic features can unintentionally lead to the subconscious assumption of lower trustworthiness, completely independent of the truth of the account given.",
